Z||000000||Huck||10-25-2001||06:17 PM||||What is the name of the small black box mounted on the rearmost passenger side of the 2.8 v6? it has a small vaccuum tube and I believe 2 wiring harnesses on it... I think mine is done, cause my car basically stalls as soon as you start it up, but when I take the sensor off and plug the vaccuum hose with my thumb, it runs nearly normal again.<P>Sorry for the quite vague description, but I am not completely familiar with the technical aspect of our cars.<P>Any help is greatly appreciated.<P>Huck<BR>87 GT t-tops||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-25-2001||06:25 PM||||Does it bolt to the intake plenum, with a vacuum "tee" that plugs into its underneath side? If that's what you're referring to, it's the MAP (manifold absolute pressure) sensor.  ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Huck||10-25-2001||06:39 PM||||yeah, thats the one.  Can I plug the vaccuum hose to get around till I get a new sensor? or will this screw things up and leave me stranded on the side of the road...<P>Huck||||reg||1
Z||000003||samoht||10-25-2001||09:09 PM||||i would look for a leak somewhere first , maybe farther down the line.. I beleive even if your MAP senor goes bad the ECM has a pre-set memory in cases like that.. I would suspect a  leak farther down.. but no you dont need your MAP sensor.. but your gas milage will go to hell and your car wont throttle right ....<P>85gt3.2||||reg||1
